-- title:
--   Weight–twist determinant congruence ℓ¹⁺²ⁱ=ℓ^{k-1} in characteristic p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta_W \neq 0$. Let $N'$ be a nonzero level with $p \nmid N'$, let $S_0$ be a finite set of naturals with $p \in S_0$, let $k' \in \mathbb{Z}$ and $i \in \mathbb{N}$. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N' k' S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_{k'}(\Gamma_0(N')))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` at primes $\ell \nmid N'$ with $\ell \notin S_0$ together with the operators `heckeULin` at primes $q \mid N'$ with $q \notin S_0$. Let $\mathfrak{m}'$ be a maximal ideal of $\mathbb{T}$ containing the image of $p$, and assume the twisted occurrence condition: for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid N'$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$ (the predicate `IsGoodPrimeFor`), the element $T_\ell - \ell^{i}\,a_\ell$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}'$, where $a_\ell = \#\mathbb{Z}/\ell + 1 - \#(W \bmod \ell)$ is `apOfModel`. Let $F$ be a field of characteristic $p$, and let $kn$ be a natural number with $(kn : \mathbb{Z}) = k'$. Then for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid N'$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$ one has $(\ell : F)^{1+2i} = (\ell : F)^{kn-1}$, the exponent $kn-1$ being truncated subtraction of naturals.
--
--   This is the comparison of determinants underlying weight–twist bookkeeping in level lowering: the Galois representation attached to a weight-$k'$ eigensystem has determinant the $(k'-1)$-st power of the mod-$p$ cyclotomic character, while the representation attached to $W$ twisted by the $i$-th power of that character has determinant its $(1+2i)$-th power, and the two are compared at Frobenius elements, where the cyclotomic character takes the value $\ell$. It feeds the extraction of the admissible weights and twists in [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_two_or_succ_of_ideal_heckeAlgebra_pow_mul_apOfModel_of_inertia_moves_torsion_of_katz_of_eq_three`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_two_or_succ_of_ideal_heckeAlgebra_pow_mul_apOfModel_of_inertia_moves_torsion_of_katz_of_eq_three).
